# Intended Dutch changes of the GNOME extension and the installer (GE1c; notes/claude/plan.md ground rule "Dutch
# stays default and byte-identical"; format of the UI's tests/i18n/BASELINE-CHANGES, gone with WebKit). One line per
# change, tab-separated:
#   STEP<TAB>key:ext.ID<TAB>the new nl text, exactly (\n \t escaped)<TAB>why
#       ID is a row of tests/installer/ext/dump.mjs (the text the extension shows or returns, in nl);
#       tests/installer/test_extension_text.py requires that the nl dump of extension/ differs from the nl dump of
#       3b898e6's extension in exactly these rows, with exactly this text.
#   STEP<TAB>key:install.ID<TAB>the new nl text<TAB>why
#       a text of the T table of scripts/install.py (or uninstall.py) whose output differs from 3b898e6 in nl;
#       tests/installer/test_installer.py asserts these outputs one by one; every other nl output is compared
#       byte for byte with the 3b898e6 installer run in the same case directory.
#   STEP<TAB>file(s)<TAB>a behaviour change without new text
# Everything not listed is byte-identical in nl: the fallback taskbar's labels and accessible names, the
# Ctrl+Alt+Tab name, the clock (%d-%m-%Y), Main.notify texts, the test notification, the two Dutch notification
# failures, the installer's six closing lines, its error texts, and the desktop entries (Name=, Comment=).
