GE1c	key:ext.appInfo.settings	Win11 Instellingen	launch-context name when the own .desktop file is missing: the Dutch name of host/src/desktop-entries.json (C6) instead of an English one
GE1c	key:ext.appInfo.taskmgr	Win11 Taakbeheer	launch-context name when the own .desktop file is missing: the Dutch name of host/src/desktop-entries.json (C6) instead of an English one
GE1c	key:ext.appInfo.alles	Alles	launch-context name when the own .desktop file is missing: the Dutch name of host/src/desktop-entries.json (C6) instead of an English one; "Alles" instead of "Everything" (D-G5)
GE1c	key:ext.appInfo.disks	Win11 Schijfbeheer	launch-context name when the own .desktop file is missing: the Dutch name of host/src/desktop-entries.json (C6) instead of an English one
GE1c	key:ext.appInfo.defaultapps	Win11 Standaardapps	launch-context name when the own .desktop file is missing: the Dutch name of host/src/desktop-entries.json (C6) instead of an English one
GE1c	key:ext.appInfo.installer	Win11 App-installatie	launch-context name when the own .desktop file is missing: the Dutch name of host/src/desktop-entries.json (C6) instead of an English one
GE1c	key:ext.failure.notificationUnknown	Onbekende meldingsfunctie: notifications.zap	the toast text of this failure was English in nl (3b898e6 had no Dutch for it; plan-critique F4); code unchanged; the dump calls notifications.zap, {method} is the method name
GE1c	key:ext.notificationUntitled.appName	""	contracts C5: a GNOME source without a name gets appName "" (the UI shows its own Melding/Notification) instead of the English "Notification"
GE1c	key:ext.failure.notificationOffline	De meldingenkoppeling staat uit.	the toast text of this failure was English in nl (3b898e6 had no Dutch for it; plan-critique F4); code unchanged
GE1c	key:install.langChosen	Taal: Nederlands. In English: choose English in Instellingen › Tijd en taal › Taal en regio.	new first line of a FIRST install only (no settings.json, no payload): the language was guessed from the locale (H D4) and is now stored; 3b898e6 printed nothing about the language
GE1c	key:install.langZone	Taal: Nederlands, vanwege de tijdzone {zone}. In English: choose English in Instellingen › Tijd en taal › Taal en regio.	as langChosen, when an English locale gave nl through a Dutch time zone (H D4; Robin's en_US + Europe/Amsterdam)
GE1c	key:install.langFormats	Taal: Nederlands, vanwege de Nederlandse notatie in {var}. In English: choose English in Instellingen › Tijd en taal › Taal en regio.	as langChosen, when an English locale gave nl through Dutch formats (H D4)
GE1c	key:install.langMigrated	Taal: {name}, overgenomen van Win11 Shell voor Hyprland ({file}).	first install over H: H's language moved into a new complete settings.json (plan-critique F20)
GE1c	key:install.langKept	Let op: --lang {lang} geldt alleen zonder opgeslagen keuze. Win11 blijft {name} ({file}); wijzig de taal in {path}.	new: --lang on an install that has a stored language (C6: the stored language wins)
GE1c	key:install.missingBinary	Ontbreekt: {source}. Bouw eerst met scripts/build.sh.	same text; now one line for EVERY missing binary (3b898e6 named only the first); with WIN11_BUILD_DIR unset a complete target/release wins over a stale bin/
GE1c	key:install.badLang	Onbekende taal ‘{lang}’: kies nl of en.	new (printed in nl and en): 3b898e6 ignored every argument after ROOT
GE1c	key:install.badOption	Onbekende optie: {option}	new: an unknown option now stops with exit 2 instead of being ignored
GE1c	key:install.usage	Gebruik: scripts/install.sh [--lang nl|en]\n  --lang nl|en  de taal van Win11 bij een eerste installatie; een keuze die al in settings.json staat, blijft gelden	new: --help
GE1c	key:install.missingParts	Ontbrekende systeemonderdelen: {missing}.	new runtime preflight (libraries the binaries need, libarchive.so.13, python3-gi, glib-compile-schemas)
GE1c	key:install.installParts	Installeer ze op Ubuntu met: sudo apt install {packages}	new, with missingParts
GE1c	key:install.noDesktopDatabase	Let op: update-desktop-database ontbreekt (pakket desktop-file-utils); de app-database van GNOME wordt niet bijgewerkt.	new warning; 3b898e6 skipped update-desktop-database silently
GE1c	key:install.configNotOwn	Niet overschreven: {path} moet een gewone map van deze gebruiker zijn.	new: only before writing a first settings.json, the host's own rule for its folder
GE1c	key:install.badTable	Ontbrekend of ongeldig projectbestand: {file}	new: host/src/desktop-entries.json or settings-defaults.json missing or broken
GE1c	key:install.uninstall.usage	Gebruik: scripts/uninstall.sh [--files-only] [--lang nl|en]	uninstall.py: --lang added (was "Gebruik: scripts/uninstall.sh [--files-only]")
GE1c	key:install.staleRemoved	Verwijderd uit de extensiemap (geen bestand van deze versie): {path}	new (ge1c-review m3): install.py and uninstall.py name every top-level file of the own extension folder that they remove and that this version does not ship; printed only when such a file exists, so Robin's update output stays identical
GE1c	scripts/install.py	a first install (no win11-gnome settings.json and no payload) writes config/win11-gnome/settings.json: the complete host/src/settings-defaults.json with the chosen language (GE0c F3), 0600 in a 0700 folder, under .settings.lock, by rename; never over an existing file; after every check and before the first change (ge1c-review m1), so a rerun after a failed install keeps the choice; its language line is printed at that moment (still the first line)
GE1c	scripts/install.py	the extension is installed as the listing of extension/ minus schemas/ (C7, F18); a top-level file this tree no longer ships is removed from the own extension folder and named (key:install.staleRemoved)
GE1c	scripts/install.py	Name= and Comment= of the 10 entries come from host/src/desktop-entries.json in the stored language (C6, F19); the nl values are the 3b898e6 literals byte for byte
GE1c	scripts/uninstall.py	removes every top-level file of its own extension folder (was a fixed list of 9 names); each one outside that list and outside this version's extension/ is named (key:install.staleRemoved)
GE1c	extension/extension.js	the language comes only from GLib.get_user_config_dir()/win11-gnome/settings.json and is followed live through a directory monitor (C1); theme/taskbar keys still use readSettings() unchanged
GE1c	scripts/build.sh	cargo build --release --offline --locked -j "${WIN11_BUILD_JOBS:-2}" (was --locked -j 4, online; contracts C8, plan-critique F34, ge1c-review m7); messages unchanged
R3-NATIVE	extension/extension.js	D-G21: Task Manager’s “Always on top” works in GNOME: while taskmgr.alwaysOnTop is true in Win11’s settings.json (read by the language watch and followed live, C1), every window with Task Manager’s WM class io.github.win11shell.TaskManager is above other windows (make_above) and on every workspace (stick), also one opened later; switched off, or with the extension disabled, each window gets back the above and sticky states it had before. No new text (the switch and its description are the UI’s, tests/i18n/BASELINE-CHANGES.ui)
FIX-POWER	key:ext.added.powerAction	Onbekende energieactie.	new text: panel.power (Start hands a power action to the panel window, D-G58) refuses an action other than shutdown, reboot, logout, suspend or lock
NO-WEBKIT	scripts/build.sh	the pkg-config check no longer asks for webkit2gtk-4.1 and the missing-packages hint (nl and en) no longer names libwebkit2gtk-4.1-dev; nl now: Bouwpakketten ontbreken. Op Ubuntu: sudo apt install build-essential pkg-config libgtk-3-dev libgtk-4-dev (the host has no WebKit since the last-webkit tag)
NO-WEBKIT	key:install.missingSource	Ontbrekende interfacebron: {directory}	was "Ontbrekende interface/compatibiliteitsbron: {directory}": the installer needs only vendor/ui/assets now; vendor/host, the Python reference, stays in the source tree and is no longer checked or installed
NO-WEBKIT	key:install.webkitRemoved	Verwijderd (gegevens van de WebKit-apps van een eerdere versie): {path}	new: an update (install.py over an own payload) and uninstall.py (also --files-only) remove the WebKit apps' own storage by an exact list (install.remove_webkit_state) and name each removed path; printed only when such a folder exists, so the output of an install without them stays identical
NO-WEBKIT	scripts/install.py	the payload's ui/ holds only vendor/ui/assets and the payload no longer has host/ (vendor/host); PACKAGES has no WebKit, JavaScriptCore or libsoup rows; with WIN11_BUILD_DIR unset, a build directory is chosen only when it holds all 19 binaries itself (a checkout's stale bin/ never is); no new text
NO-WEBKIT	tests/installer/ext/dump.mjs	no longer calls windows.hostState and windows.hostRestore: extension/panelBridge.js dropped them with the WebKit apps' window state (host/src/window_state.rs was their only caller), and their seven texts with them; the GE1c rows key:ext.failure.{sessionLocked,badHost,hostUnmapped,hostUnpainted,badGeometry,noDisplay,waitFrame} above stay as history and tests/installer/test_extension_text.py REMOVED_KEYS leaves them out
NO-GTK3	scripts/build.sh	the pkg-config check asks for glib-2.0 (>= 2.70), gio-2.0 and gdk-pixbuf-2.0 instead of gtk+-3.0 (the host links GLib, GIO and GDK Pixbuf, no GTK 3) and the missing-packages hint (nl and en) names libglib2.0-dev and libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-dev instead of libgtk-3-dev; nl now: Bouwpakketten ontbreken. Op Ubuntu: sudo apt install build-essential pkg-config libglib2.0-dev libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-dev libgtk-4-dev
NO-GTK3	scripts/install.py	PACKAGES has no libgtk-3.so.0/libgdk-3.so.0 row: no binary needs GTK 3 (the host's GTK 3 went, 14-11); no new text
NO-WEBKIT	extension/panelBridge.js	a file picker window (io.github.win11shell.FilePicker) with a transient parent is hidden from the window list (Meta hide_from_window_list), so a non-modal one, a normal window for Mutter, has no taskbar entry either (an owned window on Windows; tests/gnome/scenarios/r2d-picker.py); no new text
